# Copy to tests/bsd/.env (gitignored) to test on a real FreeBSD machine
# before a push: `make bsd-check`, and `make pr-check` whenever this file
# names one.
#
# The machine is a device of a Pleiades project that already manages it,
# as the VirtualBox lab's bsd-check is (examples/virtualbox_lab):
# PLEIADES_BSD_PROJECT is that project's directory (a leading ~/ is
# expanded) and PLEIADES_BSD_DEVICE the device's name in it. The checks
# use the credential that project holds. The machine needs go and git on
# its PATH (or go in ~/sdk/go/bin) and cc for the race detector. A linked
# worktree with no tests/bsd/.env of its own reads the main worktree's.
# Delete tests/bsd/.env to stop testing on FreeBSD.
PLEIADES_BSD_PROJECT=~/pleiades-lab
PLEIADES_BSD_DEVICE=bsd-check
